Z||000000||turbo86se||02-03-2000||11:19 AM||||<BR>hey everyone! I may have my 88 coupe sold to a gentleman in FL! Before I get emotional, I need to get a few things done to make the car almost perfect. When I painted the car, I replaced the factory 88 decklid with one from a 87 coupe. Does anyone know how to wire the two connections together? Which wire goes with which wire? My 88 coupe does have the optional light feature (very nice), but I don't recall if the 87 did. Neither have the power decklid feature. <P>Thanks for everyone who visited my photopoint page. I know there aren't many pics now, but I've got about 30 more ready, as soon as I get my hands on a scanner. ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Monkeyman||02-03-2000||05:05 PM||||What's the optional light feature?||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||02-03-2000||08:05 PM||||the 87 and 88 should use the same harness as far as I know. If they don't pull the one out of the old lid. it only takes about 10 minutes. If you lost that one go get one from the salvage yard. You can even get the trunk release if you're lucky.<P>go read my instructions about the [url=http://www.fiero.nl/ogre/pftrunk.htm]power trunk latch[url] they tell you how to get the harness back into the lid in like 10 minutes or less. Should work for all Fiero after 85.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Monkeyman||02-03-2000||08:13 PM||||Once again...what's the "optional light feature" and is this the only difference between pre-'86s and the rest?||||reg||1
Z||000004||turbo86se||02-03-2000||11:23 PM||||monkey, it has the lights under the dash in the corners, and in the trunk lid. According to my dealer invoice, the code is TR9  Lamp Group   $30.00<BR>The lights really light up the car. <P>Ok, I just went out for a closer look at the connections, it looks like they are the same, the problem is one of the plastic connectors from the decklid is broken off (more like mangled). I guess tomorrow I'll have to go to the bone yard for more parts off the 87  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
